    "verdict": "The shipped normalizer divides retention by (1 + |x| + |y| + |z|), so a fiber pays for noncommutative transport in memory horizon.  Long-memory fibers can therefore only afford a small fraction of the transport range, which confines the Heisenberg mechanism to fast-decaying fibers.  Setting the transport cap proportional to the fiber's own decay rate removes the trade while keeping a uniform, fiber-independent bound on the prefix norm."
  },
